---
description: Cryptex architecture invariants and milestone discipline
alwaysApply: true
---

Before implementation:
- Follow AGENTS.md.
- Treat docs/00_MASTER_SPEC.md as the primary architecture authority.
- Accepted ADRs override implementation convenience.
- Work only on the currently assigned milestone.
- Do not implement later milestones opportunistically.
- If a requirement conflicts with the Master Spec or an accepted ADR, stop and report the conflict.

Architecture invariants:
- Cryptex is local-first and offline-capable.
- macOS and Windows are first-class.
- No device is the canonical master.
- cryptexd is the only supported canonical writer.
- AI/Desktop/CLI/Obsidian must not directly mutate canonical memory files.
- SQLite, indexes, caches and Obsidian projections are derived and rebuildable.
- Runtime data must never be stored inside the source repository.
- Do not introduce a cloud dependency without explicit approval.
- Do not weaken recovery, provenance, security or offline operation for convenience.

Never report a feature as working unless it has actually been verified.
